<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Sagrajas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1086</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Sagrajas, Zallaca · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Sagrajas, called Zallaca in Arabic, was fought on 23 October 1086 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/badajoz">Badajoz</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yusuf-ibn-tashfin">Yusuf ibn Tashfin</a>'s Almoravid army shattered the forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-vi-of-castile">Alfonso VI of Castile</a>. The victory showed the effectiveness of Almoravid Saharan tactics, including drums and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camel">camels</a>. It preserved Muslim political control over southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> and brought <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-andalus">al-Andalus</a> under the influence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-sagrajas.jpg" alt="Battle of Sagrajas" width="320" height="363" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roque Gameiro · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Batalha_de_Zalaka_-_Hist%C3%B3ria_de_Portugal,_popular_e_ilustrada.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
